    {
      "id": "acme-pm5300-en",
      "title": "ACME PM5300 power meter (English, text-layer PDF)",
      "format": "pdf",
      "media_type": "application/pdf",
      "language": "en",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "content": "ACME PM5300 Series Power Meter\nUser Manual, Revision 2.1\n\n1 Overview\nThe PM5300 measures three-phase voltage, current, power, frequency and energy.\nIt communicates over Ethernet using Modbus TCP on port 502 (unit identifier 1).\nRegister addresses in this manual are zero-based Modbus holding register\naddresses unless stated otherwise. Multi-register values are transmitted with\nthe most significant word first.",
          "content_type": "text",
          "page_number": 1,
          "extraction_method": "pdf_text"
        },
        {
          "content": "2 Communication\n2.1 Supported function codes\nCode   Function\n0x03   Read Holding Registers\n0x04   Read Input Registers\n0x06   Write Single Register\n0x10   Write Multiple Registers\n\n2.2 Example frame\nTo read phase A current, the client sends the request\nRequest: 01 03 0B B8 00 02 46 0A\nResponse: 01 03 04 41 20 00 00 EE 3A\nThe response above decodes to 10.0 A.",
          "content_type": "text",
          "page_number": 2,
          "extraction_method": "pdf_text"
        },
        {
          "content": "3 Register map\n3.1 Measurements (read only)\nAddress  Name                  Format   Access  Unit\n3000     Current A             FLOAT32  R       A\n3002     Current B             FLOAT32  R       A\n3004     Current C             FLOAT32  R       A\n3020     Voltage A-B           FLOAT32  R       V\n3022     Voltage B-C           FLOAT32  R       V\n3060     Active Power Total    FLOAT32  R       kW\n3110     Frequency             FLOAT32  R       Hz",
          "content_type": "text",
          "page_number": 3,
          "extraction_method": "pdf_text"
        },
        {
          "content": "3.1 Measurements (continued)\nAddress  Name                        Format   Access  Unit\n3204     Active Energy Delivered     INT64    R       Wh\n3.2 Configuration\nAddress  Name                        Format   Access  Unit\n4000     Demand Interval             UINT16   RW      min\n4010     Energy Reset Command        UINT16   W\nWriting 1 to register 4010 clears all energy accumulators.",
          "content_type": "text",
          "page_number": 4,
          "extraction_method": "pdf_text"
        },
        {
          "content": "4 Alarms and troubleshooting\nCode  Meaning                       Action\nE01   Overvoltage on any phase      Check the supply and the PT ratio.\nE02   Current transformer reversed  Swap the CT leads S1 and S2.\nE05   Internal memory error         Contact service.\nIf the meter does not answer Modbus requests, confirm that TCP port 502 is open,\nthat the unit identifier is 1, and that no more than 4 clients are connected.",
          "content_type": "text",
          "page_number": 5,
          "extraction_method": "pdf_text"
        },
        {
          "content": "5 Front panel menu\nSetup > Comm > P1.01 IP address\nSetup > Comm > P1.03 Baud rate (RS-485 option only)\nSetup > Comm > P1.04 Parity\nPress OK for 3 seconds to save the settings.",
          "content_type": "text",
          "page_number": 6,
          "extraction_method": "pdf_text"
        }
      ],
